<title>JAPAN: Japan end-May coffee stocks up 31.18 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan end-May coffee stocks up 31.18 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese warehouse coffee stocks totalled 72,487 tonnes at the end of May, up 31.18 percent from the year earlier period, the Agriculture Ministry said on Monday.  </p>
<p>At the end of May 1996, stocks in Japan, the world's third-biggest coffee consumer after the United States and Germany, stood at 55,257 tonnes, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Details of the coffee stocks were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			May 97	  April 97    May 96</p>
<p> Brazil	     16,625	  14,730	10,283</p>
<p> Colombia	   12,089	  13,227	15,490</p>
<p> Indonesia	  11,942	  11,213	 8,306</p>
<p> Central America  17,725	  14,422	 8,676</p>
<p> Others	     14,106	  13,706	12,502</p>
<p> Total		72,487	  67,298	55,257</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
